{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"externalID":"AmplitudeEncoding","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"AmplitudeEncoding"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"AmplitudeEncoding","role":"collection"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Amplitude","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeRegion","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Amplitude"},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to an Amplitude project through its HTTP V2 API."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":") for your Amplitude project in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the API key, posts to the HTTP V2 endpoint of the project’s data residency ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeRegion"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":", and splits each batch to Amplitude’s limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":"): 10 events and 1 MB a request, which a project on any plan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepts. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The API key goes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the body, so no header field is needed, and no trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves this module out; import it on its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in Amplitude’s default data center or its EU"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, and an event posted to the other doesn’t reach it, so you pick the region on purpose. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factory throws "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":" for an empty key, and for an Amplitude Experiment deployment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key, which isn’t the project’s API key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous device. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the sessions enricher, and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that session’s start in Unix milliseconds; a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record with no session is sent under its own record identifier, with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". No ","type":"text"},{"code":"user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is sent. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the record’s timestamp in epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context aren’t sent, nor is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the standard context is sent as Amplitude’s own fields","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"app_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"device_model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"language","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"platform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"os_name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"os_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Amplitude counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and bills by monthly tracked users, so each session counts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as one tracked user, and so does each record sent without a session.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with, into"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"event_properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name Amplitude keeps for its own ("},{"code":"[Amplitude] …","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$groupidentify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event isn’t "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for a request. The destination reports each as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to PostHog, use "},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import AmplitudeEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let amplitude = try HTTPDestination.amplitude(","    apiKey: apiKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: amplitude)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Amplitude receives, and why, in more detail."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeEncodingError":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeEncodingError"}],"title":"AmplitudeEncodingError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeEncodingError"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplitudeencodingerror"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"amplitude","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"apiKey","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"region","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AmplitudeRegion","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:17AmplitudeEncoding0A6RegionO"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackingPlan","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"AmplitudeSetupError","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:17AmplitudeEncoding0A10SetupErrorO"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"typeIdentifi